{title: In the Shadow of Your Wings}
{subtitle: Psalms 57:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I fled the king into a [Eb]hidden cave
[Gm7]My heart was heavy with the [Eb]weight of fear
[Bb]I hide myself within this [Eb]narrow place
And cry out [Gm7]loud for [F]you to draw [Eb]near
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm7]I call to [Bb/D]God Most High [Eb]who rules above
[Cm7]To God who ful[Bb/D]fills his pur[Eb]pose for me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Have mercy on me [Eb]O God have mercy on [Gm7]me
For in you my soul takes [F]refuge
In [Bb]the shadow of your wings [Eb]I will take refuge
[Gm7]Until the [F]destroying [Eb]storms pass [Bb]by [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He sends from heaven and saves [Eb]me today
[Gm7]He rebukes the one who tramples [Eb]me down
[Bb]Steadfast love and faithfulness come [Eb]my way
To protect [Gm7]me in [F]this sacred [Eb]ground
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Pre-Chorus (repeat)}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Have mercy on me [Eb]O God have mercy on [Gm7]me
For in you my soul takes [F]refuge
[Bb]In the shadow of your wings [Eb]I will take refuge
[Gm7]Until the [F]destroying [Eb]storms pass [Gm7]by
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]My soul lies down among [Bb]wild lions
[F]Breathing out fire and sharp [Gm7]teeth
But [Eb]your arms are wider than their [Bb]claws
And your [F]voice is strong and [Eb]sweet
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Have mercy on me [Eb]O God have mercy on [Gm7]me
For in you my soul takes [F]refuge
[Bb]In the shadow of your wings [Eb]I will take refuge
[Gm7]Until the [F]destroying [Eb]storms pass [Bb]by [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Un[Gm7]til the [F]destroying [Eb]storms pass [Bb]by [Eb]
My soul [Gm7]is [F]safe [Eb]beneath your wings
{end_of_verse}
